    "subject": "english",
    "topic": "eng_grammar",
    "topicLabel": "English Grammar",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The bird flew __________ the roof, soaring high in the sky.",
    "options": [
      "upon",
      "above",
      "over",
      "on"
    ],
    "explanation": "\"Upon\" and \"on\" imply contact with the roof, which cannot follow \"flew\", so the choice is between \"over\" and \"above\"; the added phrase \"soaring high in the sky\" stresses height rather than crossing, which is the job of \"above\". \"Over\" is the tempting answer and would be right for simply passing across the roof (\"the bird flew over the roof and away\").",
