    "topic": "eng_grammar",
    "topicLabel": "English Grammar",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The letter must be mailed __________ Monday.",
    "options": [
      "on",
      "until",
      "by",
      "at"
    ],
    "explanation": "\"Must be mailed\" states a deadline, and the preposition for a deadline is \"by\" - i.e. not later than Monday. \"On Monday\" is grammatical but would name the exact posting day rather than a limit, and \"until\" wrongly suggests the mailing continues up to Monday.",
