    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The Mughal Emperor Jehangir issued a Farman (royal decree), permitting the English to establish a factory at Surat in -",
    "options": [
      "1611",
      "1613",
      "1615",
      "1617"
    ],
    "explanation": "Jahangir's farman of 1613 permitted the English East India Company to set up its first factory (trading post) at Surat.\n\n💡 Think of it like a landlord finally handing over the shop keys in 1613 -- the English had been asking (via Hawkins) since 1608, but the signed lease only came through in 1613.\n\n⚠️ 1611 and 1615 tempt because English envoys (Hawkins, then Roe) were active in those years, but the actual factory permission was 1613.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
