    "topicLabel": "Modern India & Freedom Struggle",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The first Carnatic was the extension of which war?",
    "options": [
      "Anglo-Russian war",
      "Anglo- French war",
      "Russo-Japanese war",
      "Anglo-Mughal war"
    ],
    "explanation": "The First Carnatic War (1746-48) broke out in India simply because Britain and France were fighting the War of Austrian Succession in Europe -- it was an Anglo-French rivalry spilling into India.\n\n💡 Like two shopkeepers back home starting a fight, and their branch stores in another city start scuffling too -- that's the Carnatic War, a franchise of the Anglo-French war.\n\n⚠️ Anglo-Russian and Russo-Japanese wars are unrelated European/Asian conflicts included only to distract.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2024,
