    "topicLabel": "Modern India & Freedom Struggle",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Mughal emperor Shah Alam II granted the Diwani of Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa to the Company in -",
    "options": [
      "1765",
      "1766",
      "1768",
      "1709"
    ],
    "explanation": "After the Battle of Buxar, Emperor Shah Alam II granted the Diwani (revenue collection rights) of Bengal, Bihar and Orissa to the East India Company in 1765.\n\n💡 Picture handing over the keys to your cash register to someone else -- 1765 is the year the Mughal emperor handed the Company the right to collect all the taxes.\n\n⚠️ 1766 and 1768 are close decoy years meant to catch anyone who's fuzzy on the exact date.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
