    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Who introduced Zamindary system in India?",
    "options": [
      "Lord Hastings",
      "Lord Cornwallis",
      "Lord Bentinck",
      "Lord Dalhousie"
    ],
    "explanation": "Lord Cornwallis introduced the Permanent Settlement (Zamindari system) in Bengal in 1793, fixing land revenue permanently and making zamindars owners of land.\n\n💡 It's like a landlord signing a lifetime lease with fixed rent -- once Cornwallis fixed the zamindars' revenue forever, that became the Zamindari system.\n\n⚠️ Lord Hastings and Dalhousie are linked to other reforms/policies, tempting those who mix up Governor-Generals.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
