    "topicLabel": "Modern India & Freedom Struggle",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "In 1772, the revenue farming system was introduced by -",
    "options": [
      "Lord Wellesley",
      "Thomas Munro",
      "Lord Cornwallis",
      "Warren Hastings"
    ],
    "explanation": "Warren Hastings introduced the revenue farming (ijaradari) system in 1772, auctioning revenue collection rights to the highest bidder.\n\n💡 It's like renting out your tax-collection job to whoever bids highest -- Hastings farmed out Bengal's revenue collection the same way in 1772.\n\n⚠️ Cornwallis is linked to land revenue too (Permanent Settlement, 1793) so people confuse the two systems and dates.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
