    "topic": "gs1_history_modern",
    "topicLabel": "Modern India & Freedom Struggle",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The Deccan peasants uprising of 1875 was directed mainly against which of the following?",
    "options": [
      "The Marwari and the Sikh money lenders",
      "The Marwari and the Gujarati money lenders",
      "The British economic policy",
      "Tipu Sultan"
    ],
    "explanation": "The Deccan Riots of 1875 saw peasants in Maharashtra attack Marwari and Gujarati moneylenders over exploitative debt and land seizure practices.\n\n💡 Think of villagers finally storming the loan-shark's office after years of being squeezed by debt -- that's the Deccan riots against Marwari-Gujarati moneylenders.\n\n⚠️ 'British economic policy' is tempting as a general cause of rural distress, but the riot's direct target was the moneylenders, not British officials.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
