    "explanation": "The Indian National Congress adopted the Purna Swaraj (complete independence) resolution at its Lahore session in December 1929, under Jawaharlal Nehru's presidency.\n\n💡 Lahore 1929 is the moment Congress stopped asking for 'more rights within the empire' and instead put 'full independence' on the shopping list.\n\n⚠️ Karachi session (1931) is famous for the Fundamental Rights resolution, which is often confused with the Purna Swaraj resolution.",
