    "explanation": "'Ultra vires' literally means 'beyond the powers'; in judicial review it describes a law or executive action found to exceed constitutional authority, i.e. violative of the Constitution.\n\n💡 Ultra vires is like an employee acting way outside their job description — the court steps in and says 'that's beyond what you were allowed to do'.\n\n⚠️ 'Against the law' sounds like a fine plain-English match, but the precise constitutional-law meaning is about exceeding granted powers/violating the Constitution.",
