    "question": "Economic Planning is a subject of -",
    "options": [
      "Union list",
      "State list",
      "Concurrent list",
      "Not in a particular list"
    ],
    "explanation": "'Economic and Social Planning' is Entry 20 of the Concurrent List, so both Union and State legislatures can legislate on it.\n\n💡 Planning is like a shared kitchen in a shared house — both the Centre and the States are allowed to cook (legislate) in it.\n\n⚠️ Since planning is largely driven by the Centre (old Planning Commission, now NITI Aayog), it's tempting to assume it belongs solely to the Union List.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
