    "explanation": "After the Planning Commission was replaced by NITI Aayog, a NITI Aayog task force has been mandated to review and recommend the methodology for poverty estimation in India.\n\n💡 Think of NSSO as the surveyor going door-to-door collecting data, while the NITI Aayog task force is the committee that decides what that data actually means for the poverty line.\n\n⚠️ NSSO is tempting because it collects the underlying consumption-expenditure survey data used in the estimation, but the estimation/methodology task itself sits with the NITI Aayog task force.",
