    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Which of the following is a chemical change?",
    "options": [
      "Melting of ice",
      "Boiling of water",
      "Dissolving sugar in water",
      "Rusting of iron"
    ],
    "explanation": "Rusting of iron forms a new substance (iron oxide) through a chemical reaction with oxygen and moisture, unlike the other options which are reversible physical changes.\n\n💡 Melting ice or boiling water is like folding and unfolding a paper — same substance, different shape. Rusting is like burning that paper — you get a genuinely new material you can't turn back.\n\n⚠️ Boiling water or melting ice feel like 'big transformations' visually, but nothing new is chemically formed — they're just state changes.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
