    "question": "The technology developed by Dr Lalji Singh that found wide application in forensic investigation is -",
    "options": [
      "DNA finger printing technology",
      "Restriction enzyme technology",
      "DNA barcoding technology",
      "Whole genome sequencing technology"
    ],
    "explanation": "Dr Lalji Singh developed DNA fingerprinting in India, using the Bkm-derived Bnd 2 probe at CCMB Hyderabad, and the technique was first accepted as evidence by an Indian court in 1989. He is remembered as the father of Indian DNA fingerprinting, later headed CCMB and served as Vice-Chancellor of BHU, and received the Padma Shri in 2004. DNA barcoding and whole-genome sequencing are later, distinct technologies used mainly for species identification and full genome reading rather than individual identification in casework.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
