    "question": "Right : Duty: : Power : ?",
    "options": [
      "Wrong",
      "Powerless",
      "Weak",
      "Liability"
    ],
    "explanation": "This tests Hohfeld's jural correlatives, the standard jurisprudence pairs: a right in one person implies a duty in another, and in exactly the same way a power in one person implies a liability in another. So Power corresponds to Liability, not to any of the mere opposites offered. The opposite-style distractors (Powerless, Weak) fail because Right and Duty are not opposites either; they are two sides of the same legal relation.",
