    "question": "The Governor in the State possesses the following powers and functions (i) Financial (ii) Military (iii) Judicial (iv) Emergency Select the correct answer using the codes given below:",
    "options": [
      "(i), (ii) and (iii) only",
      "(i) and (iii) only",
      "(ii) and (iv) only",
      "(iii) and (iv) only"
    ],
    "explanation": "A Governor's recognised powers are Executive, Legislative, Financial, and Judicial (such as the pardoning power); military command and declaring emergencies are Union/President subjects, not the Governor's.\n\n💡 The Governor is like a store manager who can approve budgets and settle a customer complaint (financial, judicial) but has no say over the army or company-wide crisis declarations.\n\n⚠️ Emergency feels Governor-related because Governors report on state breakdowns under Article 356, but the actual emergency power belongs to the President.",
