    "id": "mpsc-inspector-of-excise-&-narcotics-2025-gs-ii-q021",
    "subject": "economics",
    "topic": "gs2_economy",
    "topicLabel": "Indian Economy",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "Consider the following statements: (i) Harrod – Domar model was adopted in 1st Five Year Plan. (ii) Nehru – Mahalanobis model was adopted in 2nd Five Year Plan. (iii) Gadgil model was adopted in 5th Five Year Plan. (iv) Rao-Manmohan Singh model was adopted in 8th Five Year Plan. Which of the statements given above are correct?",
    "options": [
      "(i), (ii) and (iii) only",
      "(ii), (iii) and (iv) only",
      "(i), (ii) and (iv) only",
      "(i), (ii), (iii) and (iv)"
    ],
    "explanation": "Harrod-Domar (1st Plan) and Nehru-Mahalanobis (2nd Plan) are correctly matched, and the Rao-Manmohan reform approach underpins the 8th Plan (1992-97); the Gadgil formula, however, is tied to resource devolution from the 4th Plan onward, not the 5th.\n\n💡 It's like crediting the wrong chef for a dish that actually debuted one menu-cycle earlier — the Gadgil formula's 'debut' is misdated here.\n\n⚠️ The Gadgil name naturally pairs with development planning, making the wrong plan-number attachment easy to accept without checking.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2025,
    "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-excise-&-narcotics-2025-gs-ii",
    "answerIndex": 2,
    "answerSource": "official",
