    "subject": "economics",
    "topic": "gs2_economy",
    "topicLabel": "Indian Economy",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "What fiscal policy response did the Government of India undertake in recent times in response to the aggravated global supply disruptions? (i) Decreasing food and fertilizers subsidies. (ii) Increasing taxes on fuel and imported products. (iii) Reducing taxes on fuel and certain imported products. Select the correct answer from the codes given below:",
    "options": [
      "Only (iii)",
      "Only (i)",
      "Only (ii)",
      "None of the above."
    ],
    "explanation": "To ease inflation from global supply disruptions, India cut excise duty on petrol/diesel and reduced import duties on some items, rather than raising taxes or cutting subsidies.\n\n💡 It's like a shopkeeper lowering prices during a supply crunch to keep customers coming, instead of hiking prices further.\n\n⚠️ Increasing fuel taxes might feel like the government's typical revenue instinct, but the actual 2021-22 response moved the opposite way to cushion consumers.",
