    "subject": "economics",
    "topic": "gs2_economy",
    "topicLabel": "Indian Economy",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "A condition which occurs due to deprivation from basic human needs like food, shelter based on minimum costs without considering social norms is called:",
    "options": [
      "Relative poverty",
      "Absolute poverty",
      "Situational poverty",
      "Generational poverty"
    ],
    "explanation": "Absolute poverty is defined by a bare minimum-needs threshold (food, shelter, clothing) regardless of surrounding social context, unlike relative poverty which compares against others' living standards.\n\n💡 Absolute poverty is a fixed finish line everyone must cross (minimum needs); relative poverty is a moving line based on how far behind you are from your neighbours.\n\n⚠️ Relative poverty is the more commonly discussed term, but it explicitly factors in social comparison, which this definition excludes.",
