    "topicLabel": "Mizoram GK",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "India’s Deep Ocean Mission involves the development of technologies for mining Polymetallic Nodules from the seabed. These nodules are of significant economic interest primarily due to their high concentration of:",
    "options": [
      "Gold and Silver.",
      "Iron and Aluminum.",
      "Nickel, Copper, Cobalt, and Manganese.",
      "Thorium and Uranium."
    ],
    "explanation": "Polymetallic nodules on the deep seabed are potato-shaped concretions rich in nickel, copper, cobalt and manganese — metals critical for batteries and steel alloys.\n\n💡 Picture the ocean floor scattered with lumpy \"metal potatoes\" instead of real potatoes — mining them is harvesting a hidden crop of battery metals.\n\n⚠️ \"Gold and Silver\" sounds like the obvious precious-metal answer, but nodules are prized for base/battery metals, not precious ones.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2025,
    "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-excise-&-narcotics-2025-gs-iii",
    "answerIndex": 2,
