    "id": "mpsc-inspector-of-excise-&-narcotics-2025-gs-iii-q012",
    "subject": "gk",
    "topic": "gs3_mizoram",
    "topicLabel": "Mizoram GK",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The Unified Payments Interface (UPI) has revolutionized digital payments in India. A key technical feature that enables its high volume of real-time transactions is its:",
    "options": [
      "Dependence on a centralized server managed by the Reserve Bank of India.",
      "Use of a distributed ledger system similar to blockchain.",
      "Operation as a single-bank, closed-loop system for security.",
      "Three-tier architecture that decouples the payment service provider from the bank’s core banking system."
    ],
    "explanation": "UPI's three-tier architecture separates the app layer (PSP), the NPCI switch, and banks' core banking systems, letting millions of transactions route in parallel without overloading any one bank's servers.\n\n💡 It's like a restaurant with separate order-takers, kitchen, and cashier instead of one person doing everything — splitting the job lets UPI serve huge crowds at once.\n\n⚠️ \"Distributed ledger system similar to blockchain\" sounds techy and fintech-ish, but UPI doesn't use blockchain — it's a centralized layered system.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
    "year": 2025,
    "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-excise-&-narcotics-2025-gs-iii",
    "answerIndex": 3,
