    "topicLabel": "Mizoram GK",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The ‘Astra’ missile, a key asset of the Indian Air Force, represents a significant indigenous achievement in missile technology. Its defining characteristic is that it is a/an:",
    "options": [
      "Anti-tank guided missile with ‘fire-and-forget’ capability.",
      "Supersonic cruise missile launched from multiple platforms.",
      "Beyond-Visual-Range (BVR) Air-to-Air Missile.",
      "Submarine-launched ballistic missile."
    ],
    "explanation": "Astra is India's indigenously developed air-to-air missile that can engage enemy aircraft beyond visual range, launched from IAF jets like the Su-30MKI and Tejas.\n\n💡 Think of it as a guided arrow that hits a target the archer can't even see yet.\n\n⚠️ \"Anti-tank guided missile\" is tempting because 'fire-and-forget' is a commonly cited missile feature, but Astra is air-to-air, not anti-tank.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
