    "topicLabel": "Mizoram GK",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "question": "The ‘SAMARTH Udyog Bharat 4.0’ is an initiative by the Department of Heavy Industry to promote Industry 4.0 in India. It focuses on the development of interconnected systems where manufacturing efficiency is enhanced by bridging the gap between:",
    "options": [
      "Traditional craftsmanship and modern design.",
      "Large-scale industries and Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises (MSMEs).",
      "The physical world of industrial machinery and the digital world of data and analytics.",
      "Public sector manufacturing units and private sector technology providers."
    ],
    "explanation": "SAMARTH Udyog Bharat 4.0 promotes \"smart manufacturing\" by connecting physical factory machines with digital data systems (IoT, analytics) so Indian industry can adopt Industry 4.0 practices.\n\n💡 It's like giving old factory machines a smartphone so they can \"talk\" to computers about their own performance.\n\n⚠️ \"Large-scale industries and MSMEs\" sounds plausible given the common MSME-upliftment theme, but SAMARTH's real bridge is machine-to-data, not big-industry-to-MSME.",
    "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
