    "question": "Which is the odd word out?",
    "options": [
      "Murmur",
      "Whisper",
      "Hearken",
      "Burble"
    ],
    "explanation": "Murmur, whisper and burble all describe making soft sounds, while \"hearken\" means to listen attentively — a completely different action.\n\n💡 Three words are about talking softly, one word is about listening hard — hearken is the odd guest who came to hear the party, not join the whispering.",
